--TEST--
A parameter written as `mixed` keeps its errors: assigning it to a `string` variable and returning it from a method declared `string` both report — `rule:types/one-mistake-reports-once`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Shop {
    // `mixed` is what the program wrote. Assigning it to a `string` variable
    // is an error, and returning it as a `string` is an error.
    public static function title(mixed $item): string {
        string $name = $item;
        return $item;
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `mixed`
  --> %s:6:24
  |
6 |         string $name = $item;
  |                        ^^^^^ this is `mixed`

error[E0403]: this method declares `string` but returns `mixed`
  --> %s:7:16
  |
7 |         return $item;
  |                ^^^^^ this is `mixed`

error: aborting due to 2 errors
